fcpi patch 0001: NuQ sender survives a broker outage (review finding R2, PC-NUQ-CONNECT)
Upstream 7666c1f9, apps/api/src/services/worker/nuq.ts. startSender() had try/finally and no catch, so a
refused connection during a RabbitMQ restart escaped the worker loops and ended the harness. It now catches,
logs, leaves the sender null (every caller already falls back to PostgreSQL or skips the message) and holds
reconnect attempts for 2 s; error listeners are attached before any further await. prefetchJobs() leaves jobs
queued while the broker is unreachable instead of marking them active for the lock reaper.

